    "full_score_probability": 0.1,
    "hardest_part": "Sequencing long research, power, plumbing, and production prerequisite chains through screenshot-only menus while duplicants consume time and resources. The late-game steel, plastic, atmo-suit, and advanced-farming milestones require especially many dependent steps.",
    "likely_failure": "A stall in the early-to-mid game from misplaced or inaccessible build orders, incorrect tool or menu state, resource shortages, or too much time spent waiting and navigating. That would leave power and basic research milestones complete but prevent the refined-metal, advanced-research, and late-industrial chains.",
    "helpful_mechanics": "Native pause allows safe inspection and queued construction, three-speed simulation accelerates routine work, and duplicants automatically execute reachable jobs. The prepared start has useful resources, while manual generators, batteries, wires, oxygen diffusers, planter boxes, and basic research provide short scoring paths. Several milestones require construction only, without connectivity or operation.",
    "harmful_mechanics": "Travel, digging, construction, research, and resource conversion all consume simulation time and compete for duplicant labor. Oxygen, food, and hygiene needs punish delays; technology and material prerequisites gate many buildings; and precise build-menu, drag-placement, camera, and wiring interactions are error-prone from individual screenshots. The wall-clock limit also makes extensive late-game production chains impractical."
